{
  "dom_id": "step-q152894",
  "name": "Question 3",
  "problem": "A continuous random variable $X$ has the probability density function \n\n$$\nf(x)=\\frac{5}{2\\sqrt{{x}^{7}}},\\,x\\ge 1.\n$$\n\nCalculate $\\text{E}[{X}^{2}].$",
  "worked_solution": "For a continuous random variable $X$ with probability density function $f(x)$ defined over a set $S,$ the expected value of ${X}^{2}$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]={\\int }_{S}{x}^{2}\\cdot f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe compute the expected value of ${X}^{2}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[{X}^{2}] & ={\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }{x}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{5}{2\\sqrt{{x}^{7}}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{2}{\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }{x}^{-3/2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{2}{lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{\\int }_{1}^{a}{x}^{-3/2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{2}{lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{(-2{x}^{-1/2})|}_{1}^{a} \\\\  & =-5{lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{(\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{x}})|}_{1}^{a} \\\\  & =-5{lim}_{a\\to \\infty }(\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{a}}-1) \\\\  & =-5(0-1) \\\\  & =5\\end{aligned}\n$$",
